Etherlink Morpho deployment scaffold.

This project is intended as a Morpho Blue-based fork/deployment scaffold for an Etherlink-oriented lending-market deployment. It does not claim endorsement by Morpho, Morpho Association, Morpho Labs, Etherlink, or any upstream project unless explicit written permission is obtained.

Upstream Morpho contributors retain their notices, copyrights, and licenses. Upstream licenses and attribution MUST be preserved.

This repository references the following upstream projects through pinned submodules or development dependencies. Licenses below were verified at the pinned SHAs recorded in `docs/upstream.md`; see `docs/license-review.md` for the review that produced them.

  Morpho Blue              (morpho-org/morpho-blue)           GPL-2.0-or-later
  Morpho Blue IRM          (morpho-org/morpho-blue-irm)       MIT
  Morpho Blue oracles      (morpho-org/morpho-blue-oracles)   GPL-2.0-or-later
  OpenZeppelin contracts   (OpenZeppelin/openzeppelin-contracts)  MIT
  Forge std                (foundry-rs/forge-std)             MIT OR Apache-2.0
  Solmate                  (transmissions11/solmate)          AGPL-3.0
  ds-test                  (dapphub/ds-test)                  GPL-3.0
  halmos-cheatcodes        (a16z/halmos-cheatcodes)           AGPL-3.0
  erc4626-tests            (a16z/erc4626-tests)               AGPL-3.0

Solmate, ds-test, halmos-cheatcodes, and erc4626-tests are test and verification tooling. They are not imported by any component in the first-launch deployment scope frozen in `docs/adr/0003-first-launch-component-scope.md`, and no AGPL-3.0 or GPL-3.0 code appears in the import closure of any contract intended for deployment. This was verified mechanically; see `tools/license/closure.py`.

Upstream Morpho removed the BUSL-1.1 licensing option from Morpho Blue and Morpho Blue oracles in 2026. This repository's own `LICENSE` still offers `GPL-2.0-or-later OR BUSL-1.1`. Reconciling that declaration with the current upstream licensing is an open item for legal review, recorded as Finding 2 in `docs/license-review.md`. No licensing position is changed by this notice.

Legal review is required before production release. Do not remove upstream attribution.
